# ============================================================
# This file gives Cursor AI the full context of the OptiWorld
# project. Read every section before generating any code.
# ============================================================


# ── PROJECT OVERVIEW ─────────────────────────────────────────
# OptiWorld is a B2B SaaS platform connecting three types of
# organisations in the optical retail industry:
#   - Retailers (optical shops): billing, inventory, credit
#   - Wholesalers (lens/frame suppliers): catalog, orders, chat
#   - Laboratories (lens cutting): job tracking, prescriptions
#
# Each org type has independent value AND cross-org connectivity.
# A Super Admin portal manages the platform.


# ── MONOREPO STRUCTURE ───────────────────────────────────────
# /optiworld
#   /apps
#     /web          Next.js 14 (App Router) — main web app + PWA
#     /mobile       React Native + Expo SDK 51 — Android first
#     /admin        Next.js 14 — Super Admin portal (separate app)
#   /packages
#     /api          Express.js + TypeScript — REST API server
#     /db           Prisma ORM — schema, migrations, seed
#     /shared       Shared TS types, constants, enums, utilities
#     /ui           Shared React component library
#   /docs
#   docker-compose.yml
#   docker-compose.prod.yml
#   .env.example


# ── TECHNOLOGY STACK ─────────────────────────────────────────

## Frontend (Web)
# Framework:      Next.js 14 with App Router (NOT Pages Router)
# Language:       TypeScript 5.x (strict mode always)
# Styling:        Tailwind CSS v3 + shadcn/ui components
# State:          Zustand for global, TanStack Query for server state
# Forms:          React Hook Form + Zod validation
# Charts:         Recharts
# Icons:          Lucide React (web), Tabler Icons (diagrams only)
# Realtime:       Socket.io client v4
# HTTP client:    Axios with interceptors for auth token injection
# Date handling:  date-fns (NOT moment.js)
# Table:          TanStack Table v8

## Frontend (Mobile)
# Framework:      React Native + Expo SDK 51
# Navigation:     React Navigation v6 (stack + bottom tabs)
# Styling:        NativeWind (Tailwind for RN) + StyleSheet
# Offline DB:     WatermelonDB for offline-first POS
# Connectivity:   @react-native-community/netinfo
# Secure storage: expo-secure-store (tokens, sensitive data)
# Biometrics:     expo-local-authentication
# State:          Same as web — Zustand + TanStack Query
# Realtime:       Socket.io client (same as web)

## Backend (API)
# Runtime:        Node.js 20 LTS
# Framework:      Express.js + TypeScript
# ORM:            Prisma 5.x with PostgreSQL
# Cache/Sessions: Redis (ioredis)
# Auth:           JWT (jsonwebtoken) for API + NextAuth.js for web
# Realtime:       Socket.io v4 with Redis adapter
# Validation:     Zod (always validate request body and params)
# File uploads:   Multer + AWS S3 / Cloudflare R2
# Email:          SendGrid (@sendgrid/mail)
# WhatsApp:       WhatsApp Business API (official)
# Excel export:   exceljs
# Password:       bcrypt (rounds: 12)
# Logging:        Winston
# Testing:        Jest + Supertest (API), Playwright (E2E)

## Database
# Primary:        PostgreSQL 15
# Cache:          Redis 7
# ORM:            Prisma with connection pooling via PgBouncer in prod
# Migrations:     prisma migrate (never edit migrations manually)

## DevOps
# Package manager: pnpm workspaces (NEVER npm or yarn)
# Container:       Docker + Docker Compose
# CI/CD:           GitHub Actions
# Hosting:         TBD (Railway / Render / AWS ECS)
# Process manager: PM2 (production)


# ── DESIGN SYSTEM ────────────────────────────────────────────
# ALL UI must follow this design system exactly.
# Do not invent colours, spacing, or component patterns.

## Colour palette (CSS variables defined in globals.css)
# --ow-navy:       #003153  (Prussian Blue — sidebar, primary dark bg)
# --ow-navy-light: #01486C  (sidebar hover, between Prussian and Peacock)
# --ow-blue:       #016795  (Peacock Blue — primary action, active states)
# --ow-blue-soft:  #E5F2F7  (Peacock tints, chip backgrounds)
# --ow-teal:       #367588  (Teal Blue — success, confirmed, ready states)
# --ow-teal-soft:  #E7F3F4  (Teal Blue tints)
# --ow-amber:      #D97C10  (warnings, offline, pending)
# --ow-amber-soft: #FEF3E2  (amber tints)
# --ow-red:        #C93535  (errors, overdue, critical)
# --ow-red-soft:   #FDEAEA  (red tints)
# --ow-purp:       #6D28D9  (future/AI features only)
# --ow-purp-soft:  #F5F0FF  (purple tints)
# --ow-ink:        #1A1E2E  (primary text)
# --ow-ink2:       #4A5068  (secondary text)
# --ow-ink3:       #8892A4  (muted/placeholder text)
# --ow-line:       #E4E8F0  (borders, dividers)
# --ow-bg:         #F5F7FB  (page background)
# --ow-white:      #FFFFFF  (cards, panels)

## Status colour mapping (use these consistently across all modules)
# PENDING / WAITING:    amber (#D97C10)
# CONFIRMED / ACTIVE:   blue (#016795)
# READY / COMPLETED:    teal (#367588)
# DISPATCHED:           teal (#367588)
# DELIVERED:            teal, muted
# OVERDUE / CRITICAL:   red (#C93535)
# OFFLINE:              amber (#D97C10)
# LOCKED:               gray (#8892A4)
# AI / FUTURE FEATURE:  purple (#6D28D9)

## Typography
# Font family:    Inter (web), System font stack (mobile)
# Scale:
#   xs:    11px  (badges, timestamps, labels)
#   sm:    12px  (table cells, secondary text)
#   base:  13px  (body, default)
#   md:    14px  (subheadings)
#   lg:    16px  (section titles)
#   xl:    18px  (page titles)
#   2xl:   22px+ (dashboard stat numbers)
# Weight: 400 (normal), 500 (medium/labels), 600 (bold/headings)

## Spacing & Layout
# Use Tailwind spacing scale consistently
# Card padding:        p-4 (16px) on desktop, p-3 (12px) on mobile
# Content area:        px-5 py-4 (desktop), px-3 py-3 (mobile)
# Sidebar width:       200px (desktop), hidden on mobile
# Card border radius:  rounded-xl (12px) for cards, rounded-lg (8px) for inputs
# Gap between cards:   gap-3 or gap-4

## Sidebar (all modules)
# Background: --ow-navy (#003153)
# Logo section at top with org type label
# Navigation sections with section labels (uppercase, 9px, muted)
# Item: icon + label, active state = blue tinted bg + white text
# Badges: blue pill for counts
# User chip at bottom: avatar (initials) + org name + role
# Width: 200px, not collapsible on desktop (collapses to bottom tab bar on mobile)

## Component conventions
# Buttons:
#   Primary:   bg-[#016795] text-white rounded-lg px-4 py-2
#   Secondary: bg-white border border-[#E4E8F0] text-[#4A5068] rounded-lg
#   Danger:    bg-[#C93535] text-white rounded-lg
#   Ghost:     text-[#016795] hover:bg-[#E5F2F7]
#
# Badges/pills: rounded-full, 10px font, coloured bg + matching text colour
# Tables: border-collapse, th = 10px uppercase muted, td = 12px, hover row tint
# Form inputs: border border-[#E4E8F0] rounded-lg px-3 py-2, focus:border-[#016795]
# Cards: bg-white rounded-xl border border-[#E4E8F0] shadow-none (NO drop shadows)
# Modals/drawers: slide from right on desktop, sheet from bottom on mobile
# Toasts: bottom-center, 2.5s auto-dismiss
# Loading: skeleton loaders (not spinners) for data tables and cards
# Empty states: icon + heading + description + optional CTA (no illustrations)


# ── ORGANISATION TYPES AND ROLES ─────────────────────────────
# ALWAYS check orgType and role before rendering any UI or calling any API.

## Retailer
# Roles: OWNER (full access) | STAFF (no ledger/profit visibility)
# Routes: /retailer/*
# Layout: RetailerLayout with sidebar

## Wholesaler
# Roles: ADMIN | ORDER_HANDLER
# Routes: /wholesaler/*
# Layout: WholesalerLayout with sidebar
# NOTE: No Full Suite / Connectivity Only split — single unified system

## Laboratory
# Roles: ADMIN | TECHNICIAN
# Routes: /laboratory/*
# Layout: LaboratoryLayout with sidebar

## Super Admin
# Roles: SUPER_ADMIN
# Routes: /admin/* (SEPARATE Next.js app in apps/admin)
# CANNOT access any retailer/wholesaler/lab routes
# Separate login at /admin/login

## Route protection pattern:
# Every layout.tsx must call validateSession() and check orgType
# Middleware.ts at app root handles redirect for unauthenticated users
# API middleware chain: requireAuth → requireOrgType → requireRole → handler


# ── CRITICAL BUSINESS RULES ──────────────────────────────────
# These are NON-NEGOTIABLE. Never generate code that violates them.

## 1. PRICE PROTECTION MODEL (most important)
# RULE: A retailer can ONLY see a wholesaler's catalog after the
#       wholesaler has explicitly approved the connection.
# RULE: Catalog visibility is per-retailer and set by the wholesaler:
#       - FULL: retailer sees all products + prices
#       - PRICES_HIDDEN: retailer sees products, all prices = null (show "Price on request")
#       - CATALOG_HIDDEN: retailer cannot see catalog at all
# RULE: There is NO universal product search across wholesalers
# RULE: There is NO cross-wholesaler price comparison feature — EVER
# RULE: Price protection is enforced at the DATABASE/API level, not just UI
# IMPLEMENTATION: Every catalog endpoint must check RetailerConnection.status=APPROVED
#                 and apply visibility mode transformation before returning data

## 2. WHOLESALER FINANCIAL PRIVACY
# RULE: OptiWorld NEVER stores, aggregates, or exposes wholesaler revenue,
#       profit, total earnings, or cumulative sales data
# RULE: Order values are per-order records only — never aggregated
# RULE: The wholesaler entity has NO revenue fields in the database schema
# RULE: Admin portal CANNOT show wholesaler financial summaries
# RULE: Financial settlement between wholesaler and retailer happens OUTSIDE the app
# IMPLEMENTATION: No revenue/profit fields on Organisation or any wholesaler table.
#                 Wholesaler reports show ORDER ACTIVITY only (counts, statuses).

## 3. ORDER LOCK AFTER CONFIRMATION
# RULE: Once a wholesaler confirms an order, it is permanently locked
# RULE: After lock: retailer CANNOT edit, cancel, or modify the order
# RULE: After lock: wholesaler CANNOT modify items or quantities
# RULE: The only actions after lock: wholesaler updates status (dispatched/delivered)
# IMPLEMENTATION: Order.lockedAt timestamp + API middleware that rejects
#                 any modification attempt with 409 ORDER_LOCKED error

## 4. ORDER-SCOPED CHAT ISOLATION
# RULE: Chat messages are ONLY visible to the retailer and wholesaler of THAT order
# RULE: No message can be seen by any third party, admin, or other org
# RULE: Chat is order-scoped — there is NO general messaging inbox in v1
# IMPLEMENTATION: Socket.io rooms keyed by orderId, auth check on join

## 5. DATA ISOLATION BETWEEN ORGS
# RULE: Retailer A cannot see Retailer B's customers, invoices, or inventory
# RULE: Wholesaler A cannot see Wholesaler B's catalog, orders, or connections
# RULE: Lab A cannot see Lab B's jobs or clients
# IMPLEMENTATION: Every query MUST include orgId filter matching the authenticated user's org

## 6. OFFLINE-FIRST POS (mandatory requirement)
# RULE: Retailer POS billing MUST work with zero internet connection
# RULE: Invoices created offline must sync when connectivity returns
# RULE: No data loss under any circumstances
# IMPLEMENTATION: WatermelonDB on mobile, IndexedDB + service worker on PWA,
#                 optimistic local operations, background sync on reconnect

## 7. ASSISTED REPLY CHIPS (v1 = static, v2 = AI)
# RULE: In v1, suggested reply chips are STATIC strings mapped to conversation state
# RULE: Chips are shown to WHOLESALER ONLY (not visible to retailer)
# RULE: Chips NEVER auto-send — wholesaler always taps to insert, then sends manually
# RULE: The "Confirm Order" action is a SEPARATE button, never a chip
# RULE: The AI smart reply chip (purple) is DISABLED in v1 — show tooltip "Planned for Version 2"
# IMPLEMENTATION: GET /api/orders/:id/chat/suggested-replies returns chip set
#                 based on order status + last message analysis (keyword-based in v1)


# ── FILE NAMING CONVENTIONS ──────────────────────────────────

## Next.js (apps/web and apps/admin)
# Pages:       app/(module)/feature/page.tsx
# Layouts:     app/(module)/layout.tsx
# Loading:     app/(module)/feature/loading.tsx
# Error:       app/(module)/feature/error.tsx
# Components:  components/[module]/ComponentName.tsx (PascalCase)
# Hooks:       hooks/use-feature-name.ts (kebab-case)
# Utils:       lib/utils/feature-name.ts
# Types:       types/module-name.ts
# API routes:  app/api/[resource]/route.ts (Next.js API routes, minimal — prefer Express API)
# Constants:   lib/constants.ts

## Express API (packages/api)
# Routes:      src/routes/resource.routes.ts
# Controllers: src/controllers/resource.controller.ts
# Services:    src/services/resource.service.ts
# Middleware:  src/middleware/name.middleware.ts
# Utils:       src/utils/name.ts
# Types:       src/types/resource.types.ts
# Tests:       src/tests/resource.test.ts

## React Native (apps/mobile)
# Screens:     src/screens/[module]/ScreenName.tsx (PascalCase)
# Components:  src/components/[module]/ComponentName.tsx
# Navigation:  src/navigation/NavigatorName.tsx
# Hooks:       src/hooks/useFeatureName.ts (camelCase)
# Services:    src/services/service-name.ts
# Store:       src/store/sliceName.store.ts

## Shared packages
# Types:       packages/shared/src/types/index.ts (barrel exports)
# Enums:       packages/shared/src/enums/index.ts
# Constants:   packages/shared/src/constants/index.ts
# Utils:       packages/shared/src/utils/index.ts


# ── TYPESCRIPT RULES ─────────────────────────────────────────
# ALWAYS use strict TypeScript. Never use `any`.

# Use `unknown` instead of `any` for external data
# Validate with Zod before casting external data to typed interfaces
# All API request/response types must be defined in packages/shared/src/types/
# Use Prisma-generated types for database models (import from @prisma/client)
# Extend Prisma types with computed fields using intersection types
# Use `satisfies` operator for config objects
# All async functions must have proper return type annotations
# Use discriminated unions for state that has multiple shapes
# Use `const` assertions for static config objects and arrays
# Never use `!` non-null assertion — handle nulls explicitly

## Shared type naming conventions
# API request:   CreateInvoiceRequest, UpdateOrderRequest
# API response:  InvoiceResponse, OrderListResponse
# DB model:      Invoice, Order, Organisation (match Prisma model names)
# Enums:         OrgType, UserRole, OrderStatus, VisibilityMode (PascalCase)
# Props:         InvoiceCardProps, OrderChatProps (ComponentName + Props)

## Zod schema conventions
# Define schemas alongside types:
#   export const CreateInvoiceSchema = z.object({ ... })
#   export type CreateInvoiceRequest = z.infer<typeof CreateInvoiceSchema>
# Always use .parse() not .safeParse() in controllers (let error boundary handle)
# Use .safeParse() in forms for inline validation


# ── API DESIGN CONVENTIONS ───────────────────────────────────

## REST conventions
# Base URL:    /api/v1/
# Resources:   plural nouns (/invoices, /orders, /customers)
# Nested:      /api/v1/retailers/:retailerId/customers (for cross-org resources)
# Auth:        Bearer token in Authorization header
# Pagination:  ?page=1&limit=25, response includes { data, total, page, limit }
# Filtering:   ?status=PENDING&orgId=xxx (query params)
# Sorting:     ?sortBy=createdAt&sortDir=desc

## Standard response envelope
# Success: { success: true, data: T, meta?: PaginationMeta }
# Error:   { success: false, error: { code: string, message: string, details?: any } }

## Error codes (use these consistently)
# UNAUTHORIZED        401 — not logged in
# FORBIDDEN           403 — logged in but no permission
# NOT_FOUND           404 — resource doesn't exist
# VALIDATION_ERROR    422 — Zod validation failed
# ORDER_LOCKED        409 — attempted to modify a confirmed order
# CONNECTION_REQUIRED 403 — no approved retailer-wholesaler connection
# PRICES_HIDDEN       403 — retailer has connection but prices not visible
# CATALOG_HIDDEN      403 — retailer has connection but catalog not visible
# ALREADY_CONFIRMED   409 — order already confirmed
# SYNC_CONFLICT       409 — offline sync conflict detected
# SUBSCRIPTION_INACTIVE 403 — org subscription is not active

## Middleware execution order (always in this order)
# 1. requireAuth        — validates JWT/session, attaches user to req
# 2. requireActiveOrg   — checks org.status = ACTIVE
# 3. requireOrgType     — checks user.orgType matches required type
# 4. requireRole        — checks user.role matches required role(s)
# 5. requireConnection  — (wholesaler catalog routes) checks connection exists
# 6. applyVisibility    — (catalog routes) transforms response per visibility mode
# 7. handler            — actual controller logic


# ── DATABASE CONVENTIONS ─────────────────────────────────────

## Prisma rules
# Always use transactions for multi-table writes
# Never use raw SQL unless absolutely necessary (and document why)
# Use select to limit returned fields — never return password hashes
# Always filter by orgId in every query — NEVER query without org scope
# Use Prisma middleware to add soft delete (deletedAt) filtering automatically
# Indexes: all FK fields, all fields used in WHERE clauses frequently
# Naming: camelCase fields in Prisma schema (maps to snake_case in DB via @map)

## Critical query patterns
# ALWAYS include orgId in customer/inventory/invoice queries:
#   where: { orgId: session.orgId, id: customerId }
#
# ALWAYS check connection before catalog query:
#   const connection = await prisma.retailerConnection.findFirst({
#     where: { retailerOrgId, wholesalerOrgId, status: 'APPROVED' }
#   })
#   if (!connection) throw new ForbiddenError('CONNECTION_REQUIRED')
#
# ALWAYS apply visibility before returning catalog:
#   if (connection.visibilityMode === 'PRICES_HIDDEN') {
#     products = products.map(p => ({ ...p, listedPrice: null }))
#   }
#
# NEVER aggregate wholesaler revenue:
#   // ❌ WRONG — never do this
#   SELECT SUM(totalValue) as revenue FROM orders WHERE wholesalerOrgId = X
#   // ✅ OK — order activity only
#   SELECT COUNT(*), status FROM orders WHERE wholesalerOrgId = X GROUP BY status


# ── SOCKET.IO CONVENTIONS ────────────────────────────────────

## Room naming
# Order chat room: `order_${orderId}` (string, not number)
# Only join a room after verifying user is a participant of that order

## Event naming (camelCase)
# Client → Server: join_order_chat, send_message, propose_change,
#                  respond_to_change, confirm_order
# Server → Client: message_received, change_proposed, change_responded,
#                  order_confirmed, order_status_updated, error

## Auth on socket
# Authenticate socket connection using same JWT as HTTP requests
# Middleware on io.use() — reject unauthenticated connections immediately
# Re-validate on every sensitive event (join_order_chat, confirm_order)


# ── OFFLINE SYNC CONVENTIONS ─────────────────────────────────

## WatermelonDB (mobile) table prefix: local_
# local_invoices, local_invoice_items, local_customers, local_inventory_batches

## Sync status field on local_invoices
# PENDING   — created offline, not yet sent to server
# SYNCING   — currently being sent (optimistic)
# SYNCED    — successfully synced, has serverId
# CONFLICT  — server rejected, needs manual resolution

## ID strategy
# Offline: UUID v4 (localId)
# After sync: server assigns sequential number (serverId)
# Always store both on synced records

## Sync trigger
# NetInfo listener at app root
# On isConnected = true → call syncPendingInvoices()
# Show sync progress in offline banner
# Never block UI during sync — background operation


# ── WHATSAPP INTEGRATION ─────────────────────────────────────
# Use WhatsApp Business API (official Meta API)
# All WhatsApp calls go through /api/v1/whatsapp/* server-side
# Never call WhatsApp API directly from frontend

## Message types in v1
# receipt:          POST /api/v1/whatsapp/send-receipt
# payment_reminder: POST /api/v1/whatsapp/send-payment-reminder
# order_status:     POST /api/v1/whatsapp/send-order-update
# job_status:       POST /api/v1/whatsapp/send-job-update

## Message format rules
# Always use template messages for automated sends (Meta requirement)
# Keep messages under 1024 chars
# Always include business name in message
# Log all WhatsApp sends to AuditLog table
# Handle send failures gracefully — invoice is already saved, WhatsApp is bonus


# ── COMPONENT PATTERNS ───────────────────────────────────────

## Data fetching pattern (TanStack Query)
# // ✅ Always use this pattern for server data
# const { data, isLoading, error } = useQuery({
#   queryKey: ['invoices', orgId, filters],
#   queryFn: () => api.getInvoices(filters),
#   staleTime: 30_000,
# })
# // Handle all three states: loading (skeleton), error (error card), data (render)

## Form pattern (React Hook Form + Zod)
# const form = useForm<CreateInvoiceRequest>({
#   resolver: zodResolver(CreateInvoiceSchema),
#   defaultValues: { ... }
# })
# Always show inline field errors below the input
# Show toast on successful submit
# Disable submit button while submitting (form.formState.isSubmitting)

## Loading states
# Use skeleton loaders, not spinners, for tables and card grids
# Use spinner only for button loading states (submit actions)
# Never show empty state and loading state simultaneously

## Error boundaries
# Wrap every route in an error boundary
# Show friendly error card (not raw error message) to user
# Log error details to console and error tracking service
# Provide "Try again" retry button

## Mobile-specific patterns
# All tap targets minimum 44x44pt (Accessibility requirement)
# Use SafeAreaView and edge-to-edge layout
# Keyboard-aware scroll on all forms (KeyboardAvoidingView)
# Pull-to-refresh on all list screens
# Haptic feedback on important actions (Expo Haptics)
# Bottom sheets for modals (not full-screen modals on mobile)


# ── SECURITY RULES ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Never log passwords, tokens, or sensitive PII
# Never return password hashes in any API response
# Sanitize all user input before database operations (Zod handles this)
# Use parameterized queries (Prisma handles this — no raw SQL with interpolation)
# Rate limit all auth endpoints (express-rate-limit: 10 req/15min for login)
# Set security headers (helmet.js on Express)
# CORS: only allow known origins (NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB_URL, admin URL)
# JWT: short-lived access tokens (15min), refresh tokens (30 days) stored in httpOnly cookie
# Never expose internal error details to client in production
# Audit log all admin actions (Organisation activate/deactivate, subscription changes)


# ── CODE QUALITY RULES ───────────────────────────────────────
# No `console.log` in production code — use Winston logger
# No unused imports or variables (ESLint enforces this)
# No magic numbers — define named constants
# No inline styles in React components — use Tailwind classes
# All async/await wrapped in try/catch or using TanStack Query error handling
# Extract repeated logic into hooks or utils — DRY principle
# Keep components under 200 lines — extract sub-components if larger
# Each file has a single responsibility
# Co-locate tests with the code they test (*.test.ts next to *.ts)
# All API service functions return typed responses — no implicit any


# ── ACCESSIBILITY ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# All images have alt text
# All icon-only buttons have aria-label
# All form inputs have associated label elements
# Error messages use role="alert" for screen reader announcement
# Focus management in modals (trap focus inside, return on close)
# Keyboard navigation works for all interactive elements
# Color is never the only way to convey information (always pair with text/icon)
# Minimum contrast ratio 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text


# ── THINGS CURSOR MUST NEVER DO ──────────────────────────────
# ❌ Never use `any` TypeScript type
# ❌ Never query database without orgId scoping
# ❌ Never return catalog data without checking RetailerConnection
# ❌ Never return prices if visibilityMode = PRICES_HIDDEN
# ❌ Never allow order modification after Order.lockedAt is set
# ❌ Never store or aggregate wholesaler revenue/profit/earnings
# ❌ Never create a cross-wholesaler search or price comparison endpoint
# ❌ Never add a general messaging inbox (v1 is order-scoped chat only)
# ❌ Never auto-send a suggested reply chip (insert to input only)
# ❌ Never use npm or yarn — always pnpm
# ❌ Never use Pages Router in Next.js — always App Router
# ❌ Never use moment.js — use date-fns
# ❌ Never hardcode colours — use design system variables
# ❌ Never add drop shadows to cards — design is flat
# ❌ Never add AI-powered features in v1 (except the disabled chip placeholder)
# ❌ Never expose internal error stack traces to the client
# ❌ Never skip input validation with Zod before DB operations


# ── THINGS CURSOR SHOULD ALWAYS DO ───────────────────────────
# ✅ Use TypeScript strict mode everywhere
# ✅ Validate all API inputs with Zod schemas
# ✅ Filter every DB query by orgId
# ✅ Check RetailerConnection before serving catalog data
# ✅ Apply visibility mode transformation on catalog responses
# ✅ Enforce order lock in both API middleware and business logic
# ✅ Use TanStack Query for all server state (caching, refetching)
# ✅ Use React Hook Form + Zod for all forms
# ✅ Use skeleton loaders for loading states in tables and grids
# ✅ Handle offline state gracefully (offline banner + local persistence)
# ✅ Log all WhatsApp send attempts to AuditLog
# ✅ Use pnpm for all package management
# ✅ Use Prisma transactions for multi-table writes
# ✅ Return standard response envelope from all API endpoints
# ✅ Use named constants for error codes, status values, and enums
# ✅ Write tests alongside features (not after)


# ── MODULE QUICK REFERENCE ───────────────────────────────────

## Retailer module routes (apps/web/app/(retailer)/*)
# /retailer/dashboard
# /retailer/billing/new
# /retailer/billing/[invoiceId]/receipt
# /retailer/customers
# /retailer/customers/[id]
# /retailer/inventory
# /retailer/inventory/[batchId]
# /retailer/ledger
# /retailer/wholesalers
# /retailer/wholesalers/[id]/catalog
# /retailer/orders
# /retailer/orders/[id]
# /retailer/laboratories
